              "ev-a3b3061f560b-0000-0002"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 2,
              "start": 2
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "The Federal Trade Commission sued Scott Tucker for deceptive payday\u2011lending practices and the district court granted a permanent injunction and ordered $1.27\u202fbillion in restitution and disgorgement."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Supreme Court",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "a3b3061f560bff34209f0327909e0cdbe408ebd589948ddcabc85e3290b54835",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-a3b3061f560b-0000-0003"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 2,
              "start": 2
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "The Ninth Circuit rejected Tucker\u2019s argument that \u00a713(b) does not authorize equitable monetary relief."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Supreme Court",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "a3b3061f560bff34209f0327909e0cdbe408ebd589948ddcabc85e3290b54835",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-a3b3061f560b-0000-0004"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 2,
              "start": 2
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "The Supreme Court granted certiorari, heard oral argument on January\u202f13\u202f2021, and issued its decision on April\u202f22\u202f2021."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "a3b3061f560bff34209f0327909e0cdbe408ebd589948ddcabc85e3290b54835",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-a3b3061f560b-0000-0009"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 5,
              "start": 5
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Justice Breyer delivered the opinion of the Court."
      }
    ],
    "heading": "Overview",
    "status": "complete",
    "summary": null,
    "summary_citations": []
  },
  "party_positions": [
    {
      "claims": [
        {
          "attribution": "Petitioners",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "da6febf7dfa311d8d03a94170df8c36e43ec81e4bf15055caf4ddcdfdf194736",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-da6febf7dfa3-0000-0001"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 4,
                "start": 4
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "According to Petitioners, section\u202f13(b) authorizes only a permanent injunction, not monetary relief."
        },
        {
          "attribution": "Petitioners",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "da6febf7dfa311d8d03a94170df8c36e43ec81e4bf15055caf4ddcdfdf194736",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-da6febf7dfa3-0000-0002"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 5,
                "start": 5
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "According to Petitioners, section\u202f5(l) allows further equitable relief only if Congress intended it; the word \u201cinjunction\u201d does not imply all equitable relief."
        },
        {
          "attribution": "Petitioners",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "da6febf7dfa311d8d03a94170df8c36e43ec81e4bf15055caf4ddcdfdf194736",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-da6febf7dfa3-0000-0003"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 5,
                "start": 5
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "According to Petitioners, section\u202f19 provides monetary relief with safeguards; Congress did not intend \u00a713(b) to bypass those safeguards."
        }
      ],
      "heading": "Petitioner (AMG Capital Management, LLC)",
      "status": "complete",
      "summary": null,
      "summary_citations": []
    },
    {
      "claims": [
        {
          "attribution": "FTC",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "a3b3061f560bff34209f0327909e0cdbe408ebd589948ddcabc85e3290b54835",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-a3b3061f560b-0001-0000"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 13,
                "start": 13
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "According to FTC, historical cases (Porter v. Warner Holding Co.; Mitchell v. Robert DeMario Jewelry, Inc.) support that injunctive authority includes equitable monetary relief."
        },
        {
          "attribution": "Commission",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "da6febf7dfa311d8d03a94170df8c36e43ec81e4bf15055caf4ddcdfdf194736",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-da6febf7dfa3-0001-0001"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 24,
                "start": 24
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "According to Commission, the Commission does not seek to use an injunction to enforce a right to restitution; restitution is sought as separate equitable relief."
        }
      ],
      "heading": "Respondent (Federal Trade Commission)",
      "status": "complete",
      "summary": null,
      "summary_citations": []
    }
  ],
